gh issue create --title "[Task 18.5] Documentation, threat model and the final report (Modules 1–3)" --milestone "Epic 18: Extra, Verification and Submission" --label "documentation,security,high-priority,epic:m3-verification" --body $'### 🎯 Objective\n\nFinish the repository documentation and produce the PDF report required by section 5 of the PDF, including conclusions that summarise the whole project (Modules 1–3).\n\n### 🛠️ Technical Implementation Details\n\nSection numbers below refer to `docs/backlog-module-3.md`; Module 1 tasks are 1.1 to 6.6, Module 2 tasks are 7.1 to 12.4, Module 3 tasks are 13.1 to 18.5.\n\n- Update `README.md` (new env vars, how to read and export the log, how to run the verification and the tamper demo, where the alert file is), `docs/architecture.md` (entry format and chain, anchor, detection rules, alert channel, protection limits), `docs/database-schema.md`, `docs/permissions.md`, `docs/threat-model.md` (section 12), `docs/testing.md`, and a short `docs/audit-log.md` runbook with the manual tamper procedure.\n- Write the report in Polish like Modules 1 and 2 (`docs/report-module-3.md`, built to PDF with `scripts/build-report.py`): introduction in own words; variant No. 2; a sample entry; the list of recorded events (section 6.2); the integrity mechanism and its limits; both detection rules and the alert channel; key code (append and hash, verification, a rule, the dispatcher); screenshots with a paragraph each; the four control answers (hints in section 14); **conclusions for the whole project**: what Modules 1 to 3 achieved together, what the layers cover, the honest limits (single-process SQLite, in-memory limiters, tamper-evident rather than tamper-proof, retention versus GDPR) and further work; the repository link. A short note on why MD5 and SHA-1 are obsolete is welcome.\n- State every decision and deviation (no Auditor role, the 10-minute window of rule 2, never-delete retention, unknown logins stored only as references).\n\n📚 Source: backlog SD-92 (Epic 18) · provenance [ASSIGNMENT] · priority P0\n\n📏 Estimated size of issue: L (3-5 person-days, DOCS)\n\n### ✅ Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A person who has not seen the project follows the README and reproduces: events appearing in the log browser, an export, an intact verification, a detected tamper and both alerts.\n- [ ] The report contains every element of PDF section 5, the variant number, a sample entry, the event list, all screenshot kinds and all four control answers in full paragraphs, and conclusions covering Modules 1 to 3.\n- [ ] No credential, key, token, Canarytokens URL or webhook secret appears in the report, screenshots or docs (secret scan passes).\n- [ ] The PDF is exported and the repository link is included.\n- [ ] Minimum 80% test coverage for this module (documentation task: no new code; the `npm test` coverage gate stays green on the final commit)\n\n### 🔗 Dependencies\n\nall P0 items, Task 18.3, Task 18.4'
